      "content": "It's a very common feeling, and honestly, it's a sign you've been pushing yourself too hard for too long. That \"wall\" isn't a permanent barrier; it's a signal that you need to let the pressure off. Instead of forcing yourself to write something perfect, maybe try something completely different—a short, messy piece that has no audience. Sometimes the best way out of the imitation trap is to stop trying to be *good* and just start trying to *be* something else.",
