    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but that's the thing... i don't want to \"be something else.\" i don't want to be messy or mediocre. i only ever cared about being great. now i'm just watching myself decay. every day i'm less of who i was. it's like watching a tragedy unfold in slow motion, and there's no point in even trying to fix it once the talent is gone.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The idea that you *should* be great is exhausting, and it's a heavy burden to carry when you're already feeling this way. Stop framing it as a loss of talent; frame it as a natural, inevitable slowdown. If the pursuit of \"greatness\" has become this painful, maybe the real victory is in letting go of that impossible standard. Just give yourself permission to be less than perfect, because the effort to maintain perfection is what's actually killing the joy.",
      "source": "target",
